From a5ea6bed1d6b89239d01974a4d58f28b436eecb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] prefill-lend: lend the GPU-resident weights' memory to a
 streamed prefill

`KT_PREFILL_LEND=1`: during a streamed prefill the GPU-resident weights
give their memory to the prefill's scratch and come back layer by layer,
at the same addresses, just before each layer runs (`kt_lend.py`, hooked
into the loader and the model runner's forward). `KT_PREFILL_LEND_PROBE`
measures how large a chunk fits before serving (`kt_lend_probe.py`, used
by `lib/kt-lend-auto.sh`). `KT_FAST_PINNED=1` pins the lend's host
buffers as huge-page memory registered with `cudaHostRegister` instead
of `cudaHostAlloc` (`kt_pinned.py`). DeepSeek V4's padded query buffer
is allocated in the prefill's scratch. The lend calls into the streamed
prefill, the KV lend and the hot lend only when those patches are
applied and on.

Numerics: Bit-identical at a given chunk size. It lets the launcher pick
a larger chunk, and the chunk size moves NLL.

Prerequisites: none; applies alone on tier 0.

Both window transitions synchronize the device before unmapping: entering, the
previous decode's kernels may still read the decoder weights (overlap scheduling
runs the CPU a step ahead); leaving, the prefill streams may still read scratch.
torch_memory_saver's CUDA pause unmaps without waiting. Reproduced and fixed by
Florian Wunderlich (illegal address on both ranks with four cached requests
replayed together); see 05yuki/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017-ktransformers#4.

Co-authored-by: Florian Wunderlich <fwunderlich@factor3.de>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
